  "updatedAt": "2026-08-10T16:23:13+00:00",
  "note": "webpQuality is the libwebp quality each file is DELIVERED at, which is no longer the flat DELIVER_QUALITY=80 in scripts/gen_avatars.py. 23 of these were re-encoded downward in one pass (sharp, webp, effort 6, no resize) to free room in scripts/image-budget-baseline.json for five missing module images. Each took the HIGHEST quality whose mean SSIM against the file shipping before the pass stayed at or above 0.993, so the loss is spread evenly across the whole cast. The 7 rows still at 80 could not reach that floor at any quality and were left alone. Regenerating from the script rewrites every row at 80 and puts roughly 138 KB back on the budget; the masters in scripts/avatar-bases are out of git, so these files are the only masters there are."
